"""Token-authenticated desktop control for the Potato sandbox guest (loopback only).

Endpoints (POST, JSON, Authorization: Bearer <token>):
  /v1/desktop     {"display", "steps": [{"argv": [...]} | {"waitMs": n}], "settleMs", "observe"}
  /v1/screenshot  {"display"}
  GET  /v1/mcp/tools     -> {"servers": [{"name", "status", "error", "tools": [...]}]}
  POST /v1/mcp/call      {"server", "tool", "arguments"} -> {"content": [...], "isError"}
  POST /v1/lend/open|close|frame|events (mirror a Windows app; viewer page on 127.0.0.1:47812)
  PUT  /v1/mcp/config    {"servers": [{"name", "command", "args", "env"}]} replaces the user MCP servers

Only argv lists are executed, never through a shell. Argv shapes are
allowlisted: xdotool forms (key, mousemove, mouseup, type, click) and
focus-or-launch of a launcher named in the launcher JSON file.
"""

